+# Optimized rig runtime — independent harness/data review
+
+Reviewed source baseline: `763f0a9`. This initial review is CPU/source inspection
+only. No browser, server, GPU session, source edit, asset change or performance
+measurement was made by this reviewer.
+
+## Verified case setup
+
+Read ASTRA fully, the original current handover, `tools/shoot.mjs`,
+`tools/checkrigvisual.mjs`, and the current QA bridge/renderer source.
+
+| Rig | Method | Section | Compatible shared region |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| bolter | rockbolt | heading | german-site |
+| crawler-th | top-hammer | vertical | german-site |
+| sonic-truck | sonic | vertical | german-site |
+| tunnel-jumbo | tunnel-jumbo | heading | german-site |
+
+These relationships were independently read from the actual exported
+`src/game/data.js` tables and `methodsForRegion(..., MAX_LEVEL)`. Use explicit
+`hero` camera. The generic rig portrait's moving `orbit` camera can enter rock
+for underground methods and is unsuitable for matched static-camera timing.
+
+`__qa.startDemoContract` asks for `depth + 30` and can deepen the returned
+contract beyond a method's range. At depth 2, tunnel-jumbo can receive a 32 m
+target despite its declared 6–24 m range. Choose or clamp/restart a valid
+deterministic contract and record this intervention. Seed each quality with the
+same contract, requested depth, inputs, world time and explicit camera.
+
+The context exposes a random-generator object as `c.rand`, not `c.makeRandom`.
+Import the existing `makeRandom` export from `src/core/contract.js` to replace
+the QA generator; also retain an explicit contract seed because simulation has
+a wall-clock fallback. Setting only `c.state.drill.active = false` is overwritten
+by `sim.update`, which publishes its internal active state. If simulation update
+is suspended for a parked measurement, disclose that its CPU cost is excluded;
+do not describe that result as live drilling FPS.
+
+Require successful `setRig`, `getActiveSourceKey() === 'glb:' + id`, matching
+`getSpec().id/source`, exactly one visible spec root, matching contract/sim/rig
+method IDs, live site screen and correct section mode. Source keys identify the
+loader selection; separate SHA-256 evidence must identify actual response bytes.
+
+## Measurement scopes and traps
+
+`shoot.mjs:227` measures actual `gl.info.render` counters. Set
+`gl.info.autoReset = false`; production `renderer.render` resets once per frame.
+Whole-frame calls include shadows, AO, both bands, post and the isolated
+instrument pass. Primitive counts are never an alternative to these counters.
+
+The existing scratch probe renders the live surface scene/camera, then hides
+`rig.group` and renders again. Their counter difference is the rig's surface
+contribution with shadow auto-update disabled. It excludes rig shadow/AO
+contributions and is not the whole-frame rig cost. A new WebGLRenderer would
+also change material/program/device state and must not be used.
+
+Scratch renders are extra work, can compile target-specific programs, and
+alter counters. Run them only after clean FPS windows, restore all touched state
+in `finally`, and report attribution overhead separately. If live draw wrappers
+are used, measure a separate instrumented window and retain a clean window.
+
+Use raw rAF intervals, discard the initial partial interval, and retain every
+sample. Record observed application frame increments as well: rAF may continue
+when rendering is stopped. Reject hidden/clamped windows rather than reporting
+the 1 Hz background clamp as a frame-rate failure. Stable program count alone
+does not prove warmth: record program identities, `warmShaders` readiness and
+first-frame/new-program evidence. FPS never comes from the clamped game clock.
+
+Use actual surface band geometry for nonempty pixel checks. The old probe's
+hardcoded top 54% ignores carved HUD space; its alternate alpha condition can
+accept opaque black. Require RGB variation/nonblack coverage and inspect PNGs.
+
+## First harness review
+
+Reviewed the initial `tools/checkoptimizedrigruntime.mjs` draft after its author
+announced it ready. Source snapshot and expected current GLB hashes are explicit;
+eight cases are finite, clean timing precedes attribution, and actual draw deltas
+come from the existing renderer. Production already sets `info.autoReset=false`.
+
+The following corrections were sent to the author before capture:
+
+- Add independent deadlines to page-evaluation frame promises. Playwright's
+  default operation timeout does not bound `page.evaluate`. Attribution must
+  restore both wrappers on success, exception and timeout.
+- Require nonempty finite program identities and positive finite integer draw
+  counters, not just equality of possibly missing arrays. Warm-up must have a
+  nonempty completed batch with zero pending, retired or failed programs.
+- Enforce the measured rig/spec/root identity, quality, method IDs, hero camera,
+  requested depth and parked state through the final capture. Setup promises
+  alone cannot establish the state that was actually timed.
+- Regenerate the geology profile against a deliberately clamped contract target
+  before restarting simulation, retaining method/archetype metadata.
+- Record raw instrumented frame intervals and assess them consistently if a
+  paired probe timing difference is reported. Instrumented render wall time
+  alone includes game render work and is not instrumentation overhead.
+
+The known stub sentinel, simulator suspension and explicit contract seed fixes
+were already acknowledged by the author and are not separate new findings.
+
+## Final source-only checkpoint
+
+Revised harness inspected at SHA-256
+`d897255d7198734def9e52531c2145e3f001f1cb318d714df494e89f8aca8614`.
+`node --check tools/checkoptimizedrigruntime.mjs` passed, and
+`node tools/checkoptimizedrigruntime.mjs --self-test` passed all 15 CPU cases.
+These commands do not start a server or browser.
+
+Verified corrections at this checkpoint:
+
+- Frame and attribution waits now have independent 45 second deadlines.
+  Attribution restores both replaced functions on success, exception and timeout.
+- Samples require nonempty valid unique shader identities, finite positive
+  integer draw calls, integer observed application frames, visible focused
+  frames, and valid unclamped frame intervals.
+- Shader warmth requires a nonempty fully completed batch with no pending,
+  retired or failed programs.
+- Setup regenerates geology using the final target, sets contract seed 1337,
+  suspends simulation update, and fixes world time to 0.34.
+
+The author was still applying final identity/device gates and honest
+instrumentation-cost wording at this hash. Those later edits are not certified
+by this source checkpoint. No runtime acceptance is implied by the CPU tests.
+
+Runtime coverage is **0/8**. The parent reports that the single authorized
+private Vite attempt failed because esbuild was denied access reading parent
+directories and Three's relative imports could not resolve through the shared
+read-only dependency directory. No browser was started. Parent also reports
+owned server PID 41636 / port 5208 / session 59410 closed and verified absent.
+This reviewer did not independently launch or stop those resources. The saved
+server.json records the attempted server provenance; it is not a liveness claim.
+
+No retry, alternate configuration, permission escalation, model modification or
+renderer retuning was attempted by this reviewer. Preserve the frozen inputs,
+failed startup evidence and prepared harness for the root/Claude handoff. Draw
+calls, warm FPS and any improvement remain **unmeasured**. A resumed authorized
+runtime run must complete the eight cases and undergo data review before any
+draw-budget or FPS verdict can be accepted.
