+# Optimized rig runtime: independent performance critique
+
+2026-09-06. Scope: source and methodology review against prepared baseline
+763f0a9. No browser, server, GPU, Blender, or production/asset mutation by this
+reviewer. Read ASTRA, its current checkpoint, handover, live coordination, current
+export and integration reviews, shoot/checkrigvisual and relevant runtime APIs.
+Runtime results remain unreviewed until the parent supplies the bounded capture.
+
+## Evidence the eight cases must establish
+
+- Exactly bolter, crawler-th, sonic-truck and tunnel-jumbo at both high/low,
+  390 by 844 CSS pixels. Record real buffer dimensions and effective pixel ratio;
+  a phone viewport on desktop Chrome is not physical-phone performance.
+- Each current served GLB SHA-256 must equal the file hashed before capture.
+  Record received response bytes/hash, active source key (`glb:<requested id>`),
+  spec id/source, requested rig, method and one visible machine root. Source keys
+  establish source selection, not asset byte identity. GLB primitive count is
+  not an actual draw-call measurement.
+- Record exact runtime, harness, model source/shared-library and asset hashes,
+  Chrome version, launch options, WebGL vendor/renderer and any software fallback.
+  Freeze served source and assets for the run; rehash after capture. Disabled HMR
+  alone cannot prevent a newly fetched resource coming from changed source.
+- Choose compatible methods explicitly. Record the returned QA contract and
+  deterministic RNG setup, including any target-depth extension and `__stub`.
+  `startDemoContract` generates varying contracts and can extend short ones;
+  merely passing equal method/depth does not guarantee equal high/low worlds.
+- Set and read back the camera mode; retain position, projection and matrix data
+  after settling. Counted contributions are for that frustum/state, not a maximum
+  across every machine pose. Underground orbit can frame a rock wall. A nonblank
+  scene alone does not prove visible rig coverage; inspect screenshots and rig
+  visibility/coverage evidence.
+
+## Measurement definitions
+
+`renderer.js` already sets `gl.info.autoReset=false` and resets counters once at
+the start of its whole frame. Whole-frame counters include actual enabled AO,
+scene, shadow and post-chain work. Read these after an ordinary application frame
+and before a diagnostic rerender resets them.
+
+`shoot.mjs` measures a separate surface-scene render into a small scratch target
+with shadow updates parked, then hides `c.rig.group` and subtracts a second
+surface render. This is a valid measured **surface rig contribution for the given
+frustum**, excluding shadows, AO and post-processing. It is not total rig-related
+work across every pipeline pass. Report surface, section and whole-frame numbers
+separately. Verify restoration of target, viewport/scissor, shadow flags and
+visibility even after errors, and require positive rig contribution.
+
+The runtime's `applyTooling` parents generated surface tools/string under the
+active GLB root. Therefore hiding that spec-root does NOT isolate pure imported
+GLB geometry. The documented surface rig budget includes fitted surface tooling.
+Downhole tooling is usually under `geology.boreholeTip`, falling back to
+`rig.sectionGroup`, and belongs to the section render. Do not infer that hiding
+`sectionGroup` necessarily removes it.
+
+FPS must be sampled from ordinary headed unthrottled frame intervals before
+scratch probes, readPixels, screenshots or deliberate render wrappers. Retain raw
+intervals and observed `c.clock.frame` per callback; this is the public app frame
+counter (`main.js`), whereas `gl.info.render.frame` counts internal scene renders.
+Require nonempty observed rendered coverage, positive draw counts, healthy context,
+title inactive and expected live screen. Drop only the initial partial interval;
+retain long gaps as evidence instead of filtering the slowest frames away.
+
+Report median interval/derived FPS plus tail/worst interval and elapsed-window
+throughput. A 40-frame median alone can conceal a hitch. Visibility and focus must
+remain valid during the window; near-one-second intervals trigger the known
+background-clamp diagnosis. Default browser flags, effective quality and desktop
+GPU must be reported; do not market desktop viewport emulation as mobile hardware.
+
+After actual scene/quality setup, record `warmShaders()` driver-readiness result,
+then a bounded stabilization window and no new/replaced program identities during
+FPS sampling. A stable program **count** can conceal simultaneous replacement.
+Count late program changes as incomplete/cold, never performance failure or pass.
+Warmup must not require meeting the FPS threshold; that would warm until passing.
+
+Time probe operations separately as CPU wall duration and record any extra renders.
+That is instrumentation overhead, not GPU timing, and cannot be subtracted from an
+unrelated FPS result. Let normal frames resume after probes before capturing or
+sampling again; do not let a newly compiled diagnostic variant contaminate FPS.
+
+## Allowed verdict
+
+Grade actual rig surface contribution against the unchanged <=70 budget and warm
+FPS against the documented floor. A failed evidence condition means INCOMPLETE,
+not a passing empty set. A measured budget failure needs its exact state, source
+and contribution scope. Diagnose before proposing a follow-up; no source or model
+retuning belongs to this task. No performance improvement claim is possible here
+without a matched current-runtime before/after pair. Historical cold/private
+renderer numbers must not serve as that comparator.
